  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services has federal contract obligations of $686M for FY2026 to date. The company received 243 awards so far this fiscal year and the average award size is $2.8M. Obligations fell 51.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $603M in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services is the largest market, with $514M in obligations; Computer Systems Design Services follows with $87.8M. Other notable markets include Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $30.1M and Other Computer Related Services at $29M. Historical obligations for recent fiscal years were $1B in FY21, $954M in FY22, $1.2B in FY23, $1.4B in FY24, and $1.4B in FY25. The dataset also shows the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $0 for FY2026 to date. Current-year totals are fiscal year to date and are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers of Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $603M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice follows with $50.8M and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $27.8M. Smaller buyers in FY2026 to date include Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation at $3.5M and Department of Labor at $1.7M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services' primary markets?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the primary market, with $514M in obligations for FY2026 to date. Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $87.8M and Other Computer Related Services accounts for $29M. Manufacturing and R&D markets appear at lower levels, for example Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $30.1M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $500."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services has federal contract obligations of $686M in FY2026 to date. The company received 243 awards and the average award size is $2.8M, and obligations are down 51.2% year over year. Historical full-year obligations were $1B in FY21, $954M in FY22, $1.2B in FY23, $1.4B in FY24, and $1.4B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $603M in FY2026 to date. Other federal buyers include the Department of Justice at $50.8M, the Department of Homeland Security at $27.8M, Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation at $3.5M, and the Department of Labor at $1.7M. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration shows $0 for FY2026 to date."
